// The sms transport through the interpreter: a message from a number on the
// list runs as a command and is answered to that number; a stranger is not
// answered at all; only a #param or an `in` variable may be set; a rule's print is an event to
// every number. tests/unit/sms.dat sends the messages.
#param Owners string = "+46701234567, +4673-123-45-67"
#param Limit = 5
#variable T = 21
#variable Alarm:1 = 0
#variable Go:1 in = 0          // declared `in`: a message may set it
#buffer Sms:160 inout sms Owners
#buffer Rp:160 inout repl
#route Sms Rp
#route Rp Sms
println("ALARM T=", T) ? Alarm
Alarm = 0 ? Alarm
